5. Rules & Invariants
Text
================================================================================
WHEN TO USE WHICH COLOR
================================================================================
#00227A (Primary Navy) + #0a35a3 (Hover):
  - Primary CTA buttons (.glass-btn-primary), active nav tabs & active slicer chips (.glass-pill-active),
    active outline toggles (.glass-translate-btn-active), active toggle switches, focused input borders,
    clickable Case IDs, and inline links/actions ("Clear", "Edit", "Save", "Retry").
  - Do NOT use #00227A as a chart series color (charts use CHART_SERIES_PALETTE instead).

#1d1d1f (Primary Ink):
  - All headings, primary body copy, table values, resting pill/button labels, chart axis ticks, and totals.

#525257 (Secondary Ink):
  - Header organization subtitle, dialog body paragraphs, neutral icons (Refresh, LogOut, RotateCcw),
    sticky grid table headers, and secondary text links ("Use a different email", "Cancel").

#86868b (Muted Ink):
  - All 11px uppercase field labels and standard table column headers, placeholders, chart unit captions,
    empty-state messages, timestamps/dates in tables, and footer text.

#ff3b30 (Danger Red) / #e0352b & #d62c22 (Hovers):
  - Destructive confirm buttons (Delete / Restore), inline "Delete" text actions, validation errors,
    API failure banners, and alert icons.

#34c759 (Bright Green) / #248a3d (Dark Green):
  - #34c759 for "Closed" status text in tables, positive diff counts, and top-level banner success icons.
  - #248a3d for readable green status text and icons on light/tinted surfaces (login success, inline banner icons).

#ff9500 (Amber Orange):
  - "Open" case status text and warning counts (e.g., cases missing from uploaded file).

Chart Series Palette (#005192, #E0457A, #542C97, #008BC5, #A8269A, #000394):
  - Used strictly in exact order (1 to 6) for chart bars, legends, and tooltip dots.
  - Series 7-12 repeat colors 1-6 at 60% opacity (rgba(..., 0.6)); series 13+ (where applicable) at 35% opacity.

================================================================================
WHEN TO USE WHICH ELEMENT
================================================================================
.glass-nav:
  - Only once per app, for the floating sticky top navigation bar.

.glass-panel:
  - Top-level content cards, filter/control bars, login box, top-level status banners, and modal dialog boxes.

.glass-inset:
  - Secondary containers nested INSIDE a .glass-panel (empty states, inline Add-Record forms, upload diff previews).

.glass-table-wrap:
  - Always wraps every <table> inside a .glass-panel to give rounded 16px corners, subtle border, and scroll area.

.glass-pill / .glass-pill-active:
  - Navigation tabs, slicer filter chips, segmented choice groups, and lightweight top-bar utility actions (Refresh, Log out).

.glass-btn-primary / .glass-btn-secondary:
  - Form submissions, modal confirmation actions, and primary/secondary workflow buttons (Upload, Add record, Cancel, Restore).

.glass-translate-btn / .glass-translate-btn-active:
  - Compact 32px outlined utility/toggle pills placed in the top-right corner of cards or dashboards (Translate toggle, Export PPTX).

Solid white dropdowns (bg-white, rounded-[16px] or rounded-[14px]):
  - Floating searchable menus and tooltips — always opaque or near-opaque white, never blurred glass.

.font-mono-num:
  - Mandatory on all Case numbers, dates, timestamps, currency amounts, percentages, counts, and numeric axes.

================================================================================
MUST NEVER BE CHANGED TO KEEP THE LOOK
================================================================================
1. Keep the static 3-blob ambient canvas (#eef2fb + .liquid-blob-navy / cobalt / sky) behind all glass surfaces —
   without the colored background blobs, frosted glass panels look flat gray. Never animate the blobs.
2. NEVER put backdrop-filter on nested elements inside .glass-panel or .glass-nav (pills, buttons, inputs,
   insets, tables, dropdowns). Only .glass-nav and .glass-panel use backdrop-filter.
3. Preserve the 1px diagonal specular border (::before with 135deg white gradient + mask-composite: exclude)
   and the top inner edge highlight (inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6)) on .glass-nav and .glass-panel.
4. Keep the corner radius hierarchy intact: 24px outer panels -> 16px insets/tables/popups -> 12px inputs ->
   9999px pills and buttons.
5. Keep the primary accent strictly #00227A (hover #0a35a3), the Apple/Inter sans stack with -0.01em heading
   tracking, and 11px uppercase 0.04em tracked labels in #86868b.
6. Keep the brand logo clean — never apply filters, shadows, or backdrop-filter to the logo image.
7. Keep transitions fast and uniform at 150ms ease, and keep mobile blur reduced to 12px at <=767px for smooth scrolling.

